---
/**
 * Indeterminate Apparatus: the piece told along its own logic, then its two
 * performances. Photos and captions: ./story.ts. The 1024 px CIVA photos are
 * never shown wider than about half the page.
 */
import Photo from '../../Photo.astro';
import { photos as p, parts } from './story';

const CIVA = '/shows/2025-10-03-civa/';
const JKU = '/shows/2025-11-19-jku-zirkus-des-wissens/';
const full = '100vw';
const wide = '(min-width: 1000px) 58vw, 100vw';
const half = '(min-width: 1000px) 45vw, 100vw';
const narrow = '(min-width: 1000px) 30vw, 100vw';
---
<div class="ia-story">
  <!-- The Bell metronome -->
  <section class="wrap grid chapter metronome" aria-labelledby="ia-metronome">
    <div class="text">
      <h2 id="ia-metronome">A metronome that has to settle</h2>
      <p>
        The Bell value <em>S</em> is worked out continuously from the incoming photon pairs, and it sets the
        tempo. At the start there are only a few pairs, so <em>S</em> jumps between 0 and 4 and there is no
        steady beat. This noise is fundamental: it is the shot noise of counting single photons. As pairs
        accumulate, the value settles, and so does the tempo.
      </p>
      <p>
        Manu Mayr and Judith Schwarz follow this uncertain metronome on their screens, so every section starts
        in an unpredictable way and only gradually finds its time.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="img-wide"><Photo {...p.slideSBpm} sizes={wide} /></div>
    <div class="img-small"><Photo {...p.clemensTempo} sizes={narrow} /></div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap chapter three" aria-labelledby="ia-three">
    <h2 id="ia-three">Three sections, about seven minutes each</h2>
    <ol class="parts">
      {parts.map((x) => (
        <li class:list={[x.n === 2 && 'classical']}>
          <span class="part-n ui num">{x.n}</span>
          <span class="bpm num">{x.bpm}</span>
          <span class="mode">{x.mode}, <span class="num">{x.s}</span></span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="dim note">
      In the second section the wave plates are turned so that the experiment can only produce classical
      correlations. The Bell value can no longer go above 2, and the tempo drops audibly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- The classical section -->
  <section class="wrap grid chapter classical" aria-labelledby="ia-classical">
    <div class="text">
      <h2 id="ia-classical">The most concrete object in the room</h2>
      <p>
        The images follow the same logic as the tempo. While <em>S</em> is chaotic, the picture falls apart
        into loose points; as it settles, an image forms. The entangled sections have abstract motifs. The
        classical one shows “a very concrete and realistic object”: a 3D scan of the experiment itself, made of
        points.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="img-half"><Photo {...p.pointcloudOverBand} sizes={half} /></div>
    <div class="img-portrait"><Photo {...p.pointcloudPortrait} sizes={narrow} /></div>
    <div class="img-half second"><Photo {...p.caseBandPointcloud} sizes={half} /></div>
  </section>

  <!-- VoQoder -->
  <section class="chapter voqoder" aria-labelledby="ia-voqoder">
    <div class="wrap"><Photo {...p.voqoderSlide} sizes={full} /></div>
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <div class="text">
        <h2 id="ia-voqoder">The VoQoder</h2>
        <p>
          Clemens Wenger splits his keyboard in two. The left hand plays a synthesizer called Alice, the right
          hand one called Bob, and every measurement changes their sound: he chooses the notes, the experiment
          chooses how they sound. Both are wired through a vocoder, an encoding circuit from the 1930s, which
          only makes a sound when both sides play at once, the way a coincidence needs both photons.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="img-portrait"><Photo {...p.keysPortrait} sizes={narrow} /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Images of the quantum parts -->
  <section class="wrap grid chapter visuals" aria-labelledby="ia-visuals">
    <div class="text">
      <h2 id="ia-visuals">Abstract motifs</h2>
      <p>
        In the entangled sections the screen holds lines, curves and points that are driven by the same live
        measurements as the music: single strokes of light, fans of lines, pixels sorted into streaks. Visuals
        by Enar de Dios Rodríguez and Benjamin Orthner.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="v1"><Photo {...p.whiteCurve} sizes={half} /></div>
    <div class="v2"><Photo {...p.lightStroke} sizes={narrow} /></div>
    <div class="v3"><Photo {...p.wideStageLines} sizes={half} /></div>
    <div class="v4"><Photo {...p.pixelSort} sizes={half} /></div>
    <div class="v5"><Photo {...p.bassPortrait} sizes={narrow} /></div>
    <div class="v6"><Photo {...p.wideStageCurve} sizes={half} /></div>
  </section>

  <!-- Premiere at CIVA -->
  <section class="chapter premiere" aria-labelledby="ia-premiere">
    <Photo {...p.caseWoodPanels} bleed sizes={full} />
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <div class="text">
        <h2 id="ia-premiere">Premiere: CIVA, Belvedere 21, Vienna</h2>
        <p>
          The piece premiered on 3 October 2025 in the cinema of Belvedere 21, at CIVA, the festival for
          contemporary immersive and virtual art. It was so new that night that it did not have a name yet.
          Philipp Haslinger and Benjamin Orthner gave the lecture, and a question round followed the music.
        </p>
        <p class="ui more"><a href={CIVA}>All photographs from CIVA</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap grid pair">
      <div class="p1"><Photo {...p.lectureStage} sizes={wide} /></div>
      <div class="p2"><Photo {...p.caseLightStripe} sizes={narrow} /></div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap wide-2000"><Photo {...p.backlightBurst} sizes={full} /></div>
    <div class="wrap grid after">
      <div class="a1"><Photo {...p.audienceAtCase} sizes={narrow} /></div>
      <div class="a2"><Photo {...p.phonesAtCase} sizes={narrow} /></div>
      <div class="a3"><Photo {...p.afterShowCase} sizes={narrow} /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Linz -->
  <section class="chapter linz" aria-labelledby="ia-linz">
    <Photo {...p.jkuAudience} bleed sizes={full} />
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <div class="text">
        <h2 id="ia-linz">Then Linz</h2>
        <p>
          Seven weeks later, with its name, the piece came to the Zirkus des Wissens at the Johannes Kepler
          University in Linz, with a lecture in German by Richard Küng and Johannes Kofler.
        </p>
        <p class="ui more"><a href={JKU}>All photographs from Linz</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="l1"><Photo {...p.jkuSphere} sizes={half} /></div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap grid pair">
      <div class="p1"><Photo {...p.jkuRain} sizes={wide} /></div>
      <div class="p2"><Photo {...p.jkuAtExperiment} sizes={narrow} /></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .ia-story { margin-top: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8rem); }
  .chapter { margin-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem); }
  h2 { font-size: var(--step-3); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .text a { text-decoration-color: var(--smoke); }
  .more { margin-top: 1.25rem; font-size: 1rem; }

  /* metronome: text left, big slide right, small photo under the text */
  .metronome { align-items: start; row-gap: 2rem; }
  .metronome .text { grid-column: 1 / span 4; }
  .metronome .img-wide { grid-column: 6 / span 7; grid-row: 1 / span 2; }
  .metronome .img-small { grid-column: 1 / span 4; }

  /* the three sections: a real sequence, set as type */
  .three h2 { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .parts {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--graphite);
  }
  .parts li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 1.25rem var(--gutter) 1.5rem 0;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--graphite);
  }
  .parts li + li { padding-left: var(--gutter); }
  .parts li:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .part-n { color: var(--ash); }
  .bpm {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 1.5rem + 4vw, 5rem);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .classical .bpm { color: var(--ash); }
  .mode { font-size: 1.0625rem; }
  .note { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 1rem; }

  /* classical */
  .classical { align-items: start; row-gap: 2rem; }
  .classical .text { grid-column: 1 / span 5; }
  .classical .img-half { grid-column: 7 / span 6; }
  .classical .img-portrait { grid-column: 1 / span 3; grid-row: 2 / span 2; }
  .classical .img-half.second { grid-column: 5 / span 6; }

  /* voqoder: the 2000 px slide at wrap width, text and portrait below */
  .voqoder .grid { margin-top: 2.5rem; align-items: start; row-gap: 2rem; }
  .voqoder .text { grid-column: 2 / span 6; }
  .voqoder .img-portrait { grid-column: 9 / span 3; }

  /* visuals: a loose, uneven grid of half-width and portrait pictures */
  .visuals { align-items: start; row-gap: 2.5rem; }
  .visuals .text { grid-column: 1 / span 5; }
  .v1 { grid-column: 7 / span 6; }
  .v2 { grid-column: 2 / span 3; }
  .v3 { grid-column: 6 / span 6; margin-top: clamp(0rem, 6vw, 6rem); }
  .v4 { grid-column: 1 / span 6; }
  .v5 { grid-column: 8 / span 3; margin-top: clamp(0rem, 4vw, 4rem); }
  .v6 { grid-column: 3 / span 6; }

  /* premiere */
  .premiere .text, .linz .text { grid-column: 2 / span 6; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .pair { margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); align-items: end; row-gap: 2rem; }
  .pair .p1 { grid-column: 1 / span 7; }
  .pair .p2 { grid-column: 9 / span 4; }
  .wide-2000 { margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); }
  .after { margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); row-gap: 2rem; }
  .a1 { grid-column: 1 / span 4; }
  .a2 { grid-column: 5 / span 4; }
  .a3 { grid-column: 9 / span 4; }

  /* linz */
  .linz .grid { align-items: end; row-gap: 2rem; }
  .l1 { grid-column: 9 / span 4; margin-top: 2.5rem; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .metronome .text, .metronome .img-wide, .metronome .img-small,
    .classical .text, .classical .img-half, .classical .img-half.second,
    .voqoder .text, .visuals .text, .v1, .v3, .v4, .v6,
    .premiere .text, .linz .text, .pair .p1, .pair .p2, .l1 { grid-column: 1 / -1; grid-row: auto; }
    .classical .img-portrait, .voqoder .img-portrait, .v2, .v5 { grid-column: 1 / span 8; grid-row: auto; }
    .a1, .a2, .a3 { grid-column: span 6; }
    .v3, .v5 { margin-top: 0; }
    .parts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .parts li { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--graphite); padding-left: 0 !important; }
  }
</style>
